msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: README:345
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"      Optimization: Optimization settings are done by editing files in \n"
"      the \"optimize\" directory. The menu just allows you to choose \n"
"      between applying optimizations only to the final chapter or to all \n"
"      the book. Say n for a normal build\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: README:347
#, no-wrap
msgid "      Create SBU and disk usage report: self explanatory\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: README:349
#, no-wrap
msgid "      Save temporary system work: self explanatory (see help)\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: README:353
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"      Run comparison analysis on final stage: build the system several \n"
"      times using the preceding one, to test whether it is able to \n"
"      rebuild itself identically. Don't use normally...\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: README:356
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"      Internal Settings (WARNING: for jhalfs developers only): says it \n"
"      all\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: README:371
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"     Once you have set the parameters and saved the configuration, the \n"
"  script is launched. Its aim is to extract instructions from the \n"
"  selected book to generate scripts, and to generate a Makefile, which \n"
"  allows running the scripts in the right order. The script verifies \n"
"  first that the host can run itself and build the xLFS system, then \n"
"  validates the configuration and lists the parameters. At this point, \n"
"  you may choose to quit or to continue with the listed parameters. The \n"
"  script will then proceed to generate the Makefile and the build \n"
"  scripts, optionally download packages, and eventually verify the host \n"
"  prerequisite. If you have selected \"Run the makefile\", the command \n"
"  <make> is launched in the adequate directory, and the build begins. If \n"
"  not, you'll have to run \"make\" manually, for example: \"make -C \n"
"  /mnt/build_dir/jhalfs\", if you have used the default parameters (see \n"
"  the layout under $BUILDDIR in the Q&A below).\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: README:373
#, no-wrap
msgid "  NOTE::\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: README:376
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"      If you run the jhalfs script directly the only function you can \n"
"      select is to display the version number by running <./jhalfs -v>\n"
msgstr ""

